  "strDescriptionEN": "Cameron Pearce Norman (born 12 October 1995) is an English professional footballer who plays as a defender for EFL League Two club Tranmere Rovers.\r\nBorn in Norwich, Norman joined Norwich City at the age of 10 and was promoted to the under-18 squad as a scholar two years later. A key figure during their FA Youth Cup campaign in 2013, in which Norwich beat Chelsea to win the competition for the first time in 30 years, Norman went on to sign his first professional contract in May 2014.",
